{#-
  Document skeleton: the Horizon Europe DMP sections mapped onto the Norwegian
  knowledge model (research.data.no:norway-generic).

  Section titles and numbering follow the EC "Template Horizon Europe Data
  Management Plan". Each block lists anchor questions as "<chapterKey>.<questionKey>"
  json.key pairs; keys are chapter-qualified because json.key is only unique within
  a chapter. Every anchor is a top-level question of a live (annotated) chapter, so
  its reply path is deterministic; follow-up questions and list items below an
  anchor are rendered recursively and must not be listed here.

  Anchors are rendered at most once per document (see renderByKey in
  _renderers.html.j2), so the first section listing a key wins.

  Selection is driven by the KM's "Horizon Europe" tag. Anchors that do not carry
  that tag but that the EC template explicitly asks for are marked [untagged] below;
  tools/check_sections.py reports both directions of that comparison.

  Questions used for the front matter (contributors, project metadata, DMP title)
  are handled in contributors.html.j2 / projects.html.j2 and are absent here.
-#}
{%- set sections = [
  {
    "id": "sec-data-summary",
    "title": "1. Data Summary",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "anchors": [
          "reusingCollectingChapter.hasMeasuredData",
          "reusingCollectingChapter.hasNonMeasuredData",
          "reusingCollectingChapter.collectsPhysicalSample",
          "reusingCollectingChapter.reDatasetsRecords",
